{"productId": "84c11700-8416-4f75-9cdd-ae0f6a44b369", "modelName": "Model 1886 Short Rifle", "modelDescription": "The strong and reliable action of the Winchester Model 1886 was designed to handle the then-new, heavier 45-70 Govt. cartridge, developed by the U.S. Government in 1873. The Model 1886 Short Rifle features a deeply-blued receiver, barrel and lever, along with a matching blued steel end cap and steel crescent buttplate. The classic straight grip Grade I walnut stock allows quick shouldering, and has an elegant satin finish. The full-length tubular steel magazine holds six 45-70 Govt. cartridges. The receiver is drilled and tapped for the addition of an optional receiver sight. A top-tang safety, adjustable rear buckhorn style sight and a gold bead Marble Arms front sight complete the graceful profile of this historic model. Like the other historical rifle models, production is limited.", "manufacturerName": "Winchester Repeating Arms", "subProducts": [{"isFirearm": true, "isNfa": false, "subProductId": "583b85d7-bcab-41b8-8561-d85653793e6a", "description": "Winchester Guns, Model 1886, Short Rifle, 45-70 Gov, 8+1 Round, 24\" Brushed Polish Blued Rec/Barrel, Satin Walnut Fixed Straight Grip Stock Right Hand (Full Size)", "imageUrls": ["https://main-images.gearfire.com/SubProductImages/96fd2553-8761-40fe-bd19-1a351516f00b", "https://main-images.gearfire.com/SubProductImages/b66c7f19-a631-4e9b-967d-9139ada2a3ba"], "isDefault": true, "manufacturerPartNumber": "534175142", "upc": "048702119590", "attributes": [{"attributeNameId": "2765db68-a9f0-406d-8fb7-5b572b01f4ee", "attributeName": "Capacity", "attributeValueId": "ae2589e9-dae6-4559-9639-4eb8403bb596", "valueName": "8 Round"}, {"attributeNameId": "7c11c5f3-970e-4119-9b86-521429f6df57", "attributeName": "Stock Type", "attributeValueId": "e282f44e-03e0-4ae2-9f93-dd5f73c65562", "valueName": "Wood"}, {"attributeNameId": "5d7cb225-7607-4efe-ad2f-d56197e694de", "attributeName": "Adjustable Stock", "attributeValu